<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
    <title>KITTY Assembly Lab · Team Prometheus</title>
    <style>
      __STYLE__
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <a class="brand" href="#"
        ><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M6 14V5l10 7h8l10-7v23a6 6 0 0 1-6 6H12a6 6 0 0 1-6-6Z" />
          <path d="M13 22h4m6 0h4" /></svg
        ><span
          >KITTY <b>Assembly Lab</b><small>TEAM PROMETHEUS / V7.1</small></span
        ></a
      ><span class="badge">VIRTUAL WORKBENCH</span>
      <div class="header-actions">
        <button id="help">Quick guide</button
        ><button id="import">Open project</button
        ><button id="export">Save project ↓</button
        ><input
          id="project-file"
          type="file"
          accept=".json,application/json"
          hidden
        />
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="modebar">
      <nav aria-label="Workbench modes">
        <button data-mode="build" class="active">01 <b>Assemble</b></button
        ><button data-mode="wire">02 <b>Wire</b></button
        ><button data-mode="test">03 <b>Test arena</b></button>
      </nav>
      <p id="mode-hint">
        Select a part. Attach it, detach it, or move it around the workbench.
      </p>
      <span id="gpu-status">Starting 3D…</span>
    </div>
    <main>
      <aside class="library">
        <div class="panel-heading">
          <h1>Component library</h1>
          <span id="assembly-count"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="library-actions">
          <button id="assemble-all">Assemble all</button
          ><button id="exercise">Assembly exercise</button>
        </div>
        <label class="search"
          >⌕
          <input
            id="search"
            placeholder="Find a component…"
            aria-label="Find a component"
        /></label>
        <div id="parts-list"></div>
        <div class="library-note">
          V7.1 body uses the supplied STL meshes. Electronics are approximate
          envelopes. Optional parts have placement-only behavior.
        </div>
      </aside>
      <section id="stage" aria-label="Interactive 3D workbench">
        <div id="fallback">
          <img
            src="__FALLBACK__"
            alt="Saved KITTY V7.1 chassis view with motors, wheels, phone and both ultrasonic sensors"
          />
          <p id="fallback-message">
            Loading the exact body meshes. Wiring controls also work without 3D.
          </p>
          <button id="retry">Retry graphics</button
          ><noscript
            >Enable JavaScript to assemble, wire and simulate.</noscript
          >
        </div>
        <canvas
          id="viewport"
          aria-label="KITTY 3D assembly and virtual arena"
        ></canvas>
        <div class="scene-toolbar">
          <button id="view-iso" title="Isometric view">◈ Isometric</button
          ><button id="view-top">⊞ Top</button
          ><button id="focus">◎ Focus</button
          ><button id="wireframe">Wireframe</button
          ><button id="screenshot">PNG ↓</button>
        </div>
        <div class="scene-options">
          <label
            ><input type="checkbox" id="ghost" checked /> See through
            covers</label
          ><label><input type="checkbox" id="show-wires" checked /> Wires</label
          ><label
            ><input type="checkbox" id="show-labels" checked /> Labels</label
          ><select id="quality" aria-label="Graphics quality">
            <option value="eco">Eco GPU</option>
            <option value="balanced" selected>Balanced GPU</option>
            <option value="ultra">Ultra GPU</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div id="labels"></div>
        <div class="scene-caption">
          <span id="scene-title">THE ASSEMBLY BENCH</span
          ><span id="scene-subtitle"
            >Drag to orbit · scroll to zoom · right-drag to pan</span
          >
        </div>
        <div id="toast" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <div id="drive-overlay" hidden>
          <div class="drive-status">
            <strong id="drive-state">Disarmed</strong
            ><span id="drive-reason"
              >Load the demo circuit or complete your wiring.</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="drive-pad">
            <button data-drive="forward" aria-label="Hold to drive forward">
              ↑</button
            ><button data-drive="left" aria-label="Hold to turn left">↶</button
            ><button data-drive="back" aria-label="Hold to reverse">↓</button
            ><button data-drive="right" aria-label="Hold to turn right">
              ↷
            </button>
          </div>
          <small>Hold buttons or WASD / arrows · Space = stop</small>
        </div>
      </section>
      <aside class="inspector">
        <section id="build-panel">
          <div class="panel-heading">
            <h2>Part inspector</h2>
            <span class="eyebrow">SELECT / PLACE</span>
          </div>
          <h3 id="part-title">Base chassis</h3>
          <p id="part-note"></p>
          <div class="attach-actions">
            <button id="attach" class="primary">Attach to mount</button
            ><button id="detach">Detach to tray</button>
          </div>
          <div class="coordinates">
            <label
              >X offset<input
                type="number"
                id="offset-x"
                step="1"
                min="-1500"
                max="1500"
                value="0" /></label
            ><label
              >Y offset<input
                type="number"
                id="offset-y"
                step="1"
                min="-1500"
                max="1500"
                value="0" /></label
            ><label
              >Z offset<input
                type="number"
                id="offset-z"
                step="1"
                min="-1500"
                max="1500"
                value="0"
            /></label>
          </div>
          <div class="inline">
            <button id="rotate">Rotate 15°</button
            ><button id="drag-part">Drag part: off</button>
          </div>
          <button id="next-step" class="wide">
            Find next unattached part →
          </button>
          <p class="muted">
            Offsets are in millimetres, Y is up. “Attach” restores the nominal
            design position. Moving parts does not edit a print file or prove a
            physical fit.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="wire-panel" hidden>
          <div class="panel-heading">
            <h2>Wire editor</h2>
            <span id="wire-count"></span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Click two 3D terminals, use the pin buttons below, or choose
            endpoints here.
          </p>
          <label>From<select id="wire-a"></select></label
          ><label>To<select id="wire-b"></select></label>
          <div class="inline">
            <button id="connect" class="primary">Connect wire</button
            ><button id="cancel-wire">Cancel pick</button>
          </div>
          <p id="pending-pin" class="muted">No terminal selected.</p>
          <strong id="pin-title"></strong>
          <div id="pin-buttons"></div>
          <div class="inline">
            <button id="demo" class="primary">Load demo circuit</button
            ><button id="clear-wires">Clear wires</button>
          </div>
          <p class="muted">
            Demo uses a classic ESP32 preset. Your actual board is unidentified.
            This is a nominal circuit model, not a released wiring diagram.
          </p>
          <details>
            <summary>Connection list</summary>
            <div id="wire-list"></div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Virtual multimeter</summary>
            <label>Red probe<select id="probe-red"></select></label
            ><label>Black probe<select id="probe-black"></select></label
            ><output id="meter">— V</output>
            <p class="muted">
              DC nominal node voltages only. Floating or switching nodes are not
              a valid DC reading. No current, transient or component-damage
              model.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>ECHO divider model</summary>
            <label
              >Upper resistor, Ω<input
                id="r-top"
                type="number"
                value="2200"
                min="100"
                max="100000" /></label
            ><label
              >Lower resistance, Ω<input
                id="r-bottom"
                type="number"
                value="3200"
                min="100"
                max="100000"
            /></label>
            <p class="muted">
              Lower 3.2k = 2.2k + 1k in series. Each sensor uses two 2.2k
              resistors and one 1k resistor in this example. Actual counts,
              tolerances and GPIO/supply ratings remain unverified.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>
        <section id="test-panel" hidden>
          <div class="panel-heading">
            <h2>Test console</h2>
            <span class="eyebrow">SIMULATED</span>
          </div>
          <div class="inline">
            <button id="arm" class="primary">Arm simulation</button
            ><button id="disarm">Disarm</button>
          </div>
          <button id="estop" class="danger wide">■ EMERGENCY STOP</button
          ><button id="reset-stop" class="wide">Reset stop latch</button
          ><label
            >AA chemistry, four cells<select id="chemistry">
              <option value="alkaline">Alkaline · nominal 6 V</option>
              <option value="nimh">NiMH · nominal 4.8 V</option>
            </select></label
          ><label class="check"
            ><input id="power-switch" type="checkbox" checked /> Motor switch
            closed</label
          ><label
            >Maximum virtual speed <output id="speed-value">180 mm/s</output
            ><input
              id="speed"
              type="range"
              min="30"
              max="300"
              step="10"
              value="180" /></label
          ><label
            >Stop threshold <output id="stop-value">180 mm</output
            ><input
              id="stop-distance"
              type="range"
              min="160"
              max="500"
              step="10"
              value="180"
          /></label>
          <details open>
            <summary>Fault injection</summary>
            <label class="check"
              ><input id="link-ok" type="checkbox" checked /> Command link
              available</label
            ><label class="check"
              ><input id="sensor-ok" type="checkbox" checked /> Range samples
              valid</label
            >
            <p class="muted">
              Loss, timeout and page blur disarm. Restoring a signal never
              automatically re-arms.
            </p>
          </details>
          <div class="inline">
            <button id="add-obstacle">+ Obstacle</button
            ><button id="reset-arena">Reset arena</button>
          </div>
          <button id="move-obstacle" class="wide">Drag obstacles: off</button>
          <div id="obstacle-editor"></div>
          <p class="muted">
            Differential-drive kinematics, sampled range rays and a conservative
            circular footprint. No friction, motor torque, acoustics, electrical
            transients, firmware execution or real camera AI.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="checks">
          <div class="panel-heading">
            <h2>Circuit checks</h2>
            <span id="check-badge">Incomplete</span>
          </div>
          <div id="checks-list"></div>
          <p class="muted">
            A passing virtual check does not establish motor/driver current
            suitability, battery capacity, physical clearances or safe real
            wiring.
          </p>
        </section>
      </aside>
    </main>
    <footer>
      <div>
        <span class="dot"></span
        ><b id="status-line">Virtual only · physical outputs absent</b>
      </div>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>FRONT</dt>
          <dd id="front-reading">— cm</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>REAR</dt>
          <dd id="rear-reading">— cm</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>WHEELS</dt>
          <dd id="wheel-reading">0 / 0 %</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>MOTOR RAIL</dt>
          <dd id="rail-reading">— V</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>RENDER</dt>
          <dd id="performance">— FPS</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </footer>
    <dialog id="guide">
      <button id="close-guide" class="dialog-close" aria-label="Close guide">
        ×</button
      ><span class="eyebrow">WELCOME TO YOUR VIRTUAL BUILD BENCH</span>
      <h2>Build it. Connect it. See it move.</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Assemble:</strong> select parts in the library or scene. Try
          “Assembly exercise”, then attach each part. Use offset fields or “Drag
          part” for free placement.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Wire:</strong> choose two terminals and connect them. “Load
          demo circuit” creates the complete example. Use the multimeter and
          remove a wire to see the checks respond.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Test arena:</strong> arm, then hold a drive button or WASD.
          Move obstacles and try link loss, sensor loss, motor power off and the
          stop latch. Release to stop.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Save:</strong> download a project JSON and reopen it later.
          The project stores assembly positions, wires, settings and obstacles.
          Runtime always starts disarmed.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Runs locally in Chrome/Edge with GPU graphics acceleration; it can also
        be served by a static web server. No login, CDN or device connection is
        used. Open the downloaded HTML directly.
      </p>
      <p>
        This lab models selected electrical constraints and robot behavior. It
        cannot upload Arduino code, emulate ESP32 firmware, identify your real
        board, test an actual circuit, measure current or guarantee physical
        fit.
      </p>
      <button id="begin" class="primary">Enter the lab →</button>
    </dialog>
    <script id="model-data" type="application/json">
      __MODEL__
    </script>
    <script>
      __THREE__;
    </script>
    <script>
      __ORBIT__;
    </script>
    <script>
      __CORE__;
    </script>
    <script>
      __APP__;
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
